alex: quick check — bumped into duplicated events when our Rust client retries streaming after a 429 during auth refresh. client lib has automatic retries for 5xx/429; is that safe for streaming if we don't have resume support? cc @maria

maria: short answer: not safe for streams without a resume protocol. for non-streaming request/response you can use an idempotency-key. for streams we need either a resume token or server-side dedupe of whole sessions. otherwise retries can replay partial output.

sam: we've been rolling `x-resume-token` in stream responses. client should attempt a resume sequence: if resume token works, continue; if not, surface an error and avoid blind retry. also respect `Retry-After` header from gateway.

jun: perf/params note: recommend exponential backoff with full jitter. starting at base=300-500ms, multiplier=2, max_backoff=15-30s. but always honor `Retry-After` if present — it wins. also cap total retry attempts for interactive UX.

alex: can you paste a tiny Rust example with jitter? also we've seen a pattern where token refresh causes a stampede and then bunch of 429s — any best-practice?

maria: for token refresh do a singleflight (one refresh per process/client instance) so you don't have N concurrent refreshes. also cache auth until expiry minus a small epsilon. we'll add this to SDK guidance.

sam: tiny Rust pseudo-snippet (very condensed):

```rust
// exponential backoff + full jitter
let mut backoff = Duration::from_millis(400);
for attempt in 0..6 {
    let jitter = rand::thread_rng().gen_range(0..backoff.as_millis() as u64);
    sleep(Duration::from_millis(jitter));
    let res = client.send_stream_request(...).await;
    match res {
        Ok(_) => break,
        Err(Status::TooManyRequests) => { backoff = std::cmp::min(backoff * 2, Duration::from_secs(30)); continue; }
        Err(_) => break,
    }
}
```

and a Go snippet for singleflight token refresh:

```go
var g singleflight.Group
res, err, _ := g.Do("refresh-token", func() (interface{}, error) {
    return refreshTokenBlocking()
})
// res is shared with other callers
```

deploy-bot: rate-limiter: observed spike 2024-11-05T12:03Z on api-prod /v1/stream — increased 429s for some customers :warning:

jun: also add guidance: if client detects repeated 5xx from a particular model or region, prefer a fast failover to configured fallback model/region instead of long retries. that preserves latency SLOs.

alex: thanks — i'll spin up a docs PR and add the snippets + singleflight advice. any recommended wording for the resume token server contract?

maria: say: "server MAY provide `x-resume-token` on stream chunks; client MAY use token to resume at the last acknowledged offset. if server cannot resume, it MUST return 410/Resume-Not-Supported instead of silently accepting a restarted stream." short and practical.

alex: created draft PR: https://github.com/redwood/inference-sdk/pull/842 — pinging for reviews and edits.

maria: :thumbsup: i'll review today. add a short note to the Rust/Go README about respecting `Retry-After` and using jitter.

alex: cool, will do. thanks all!
